## Risk Mitigation

| Risk | Likelihood | Impact | Mitigation |
|---|---|---|---|
| WDA /source XCUIElementType format incompatible with parseIosInspectNodes | Medium | Medium | Wave 1 includes field mapping transform (strip prefix, rename fields, synthesize custom_actions); fixture file validates the transformation |
| WDA requires code signing ($99/year developer cert) | High | Medium | Document clearly; free Apple ID cert (7-day expiry) works for testing; pymobiledevice3 as no-sign alternative |
| WDA app crashes on device | Low | Medium | Health check (GET /status) before each action; if unavailable, suggest restart with clear guidance |
| Port forwarding (iproxy) setup complexity | Medium | Low | Check iproxy availability in doctor; provide one-liner setup script (`iproxy 8100 8100 --udid <udid> &`); auto-detect if port 8100 is already forwarded |
| WDA build/install requires Xcode (not brew installable) | High | Medium | Provide step-by-step setup doc with screenshots; include WDA .ipa pre-build option for teams that share certificates |

## WDA Setup Requirements (User-Facing)

Users need to complete these one-time setup steps before WDA backend works:

1. **Install libusbmuxd** (for iproxy): `brew install libusbmuxd`
2. **Clone WDA**: `git clone https://github.com/appium/WebDriverAgent`
3. **Open in Xcode**: `open WebDriverAgent/WebDriverAgent.xcodeproj`
4. **Configure signing**: Select team (free or $99 developer account), set bundle ID prefix
5. **Build to device**: Select device as destination, Product → Build For → Testing
6. **Start port forwarding**: `iproxy 8100 8100 --udid <deviceId> &`
7. **Verify**: `curl http://localhost:8100/status` → should return JSON with `sessionId`

The doctor command will check steps 1 and 7, and provide guidance for the rest.

